.nh
.TH "ORBIT" "1" "Aug 2026" "Orbit Developer Platform" "Orbit Platform Manual"

.SH NAME
orbit-invite-list - List active and stored developer onboarding invitations


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorbit invite list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Displays a table or JSON array of stored invitations with their status, scope, and expiration. By default, only active invitations are shown; use --all to include revoked and expired.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--all\fP[=false]
	Include revoked and expired invitations

.PP
\fB-f\fP, \fB--format\fP="table"
	Output format (table or json)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Print the result as a JSON envelope

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=0
	maximum rows per page (0 = all)

.PP
\fB--page\fP=1
	page number to display

.PP
\fB--store-file\fP=""
	Custom path to invites storage file


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	Custom path to Orbit CLI configuration file


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBorbit-invite(1)\fP
